From Security to Determinism: Redefining SAIHV
The SAIHV project has officially outgrown its initial scope. While the system remains hardened, the core breakthrough of the v7.5-PATENT-SYNC audit has necessitated a formal redefinition of the acronym:

Legacy: Secure Artificial Intelligence Hyper Visor

Current: System Agnostic AI for Hardware Virtualization

Why the Change?
Traditional hypervisors focus on resource sharing and boundary security. SAIHV has evolved into a hardware-logic orchestrator. By achieving a 1:1 "Silicon-to-Logic" lock, we have proven that the system is no longer just securing an AI—it is virtualizing the hardware behavior itself to ensure Universal Determinism.

Whether running on an NVIDIA 3060 Ti or future heterogeneous silicon, SAIHV ensures the hardware serves the logic, not the other way around.
